# Events consumed by their producer

The aggregate changes state and enforces its rules synchronously. When the service needs a separate reaction, the command handler stages a Protobuf event in its Outbox and saves it together with that change. Use the broker for this path even when the producer and consumer are the same service. Avoid `AddDomainEvent` and in-process `INotification` dispatch.

For example, a service that records a booking and then sends a confirmation can publish `BookingRecorded` and bind its own queue to that event type. After commit the relay delivers it through RabbitMQ. The consumer uses the service's Inbox and calls a Mediator handler. Stage the reaction and the Inbox receipt in one unit of work. A replay of the same envelope must produce one confirmation. Bind the queue to the input event type so an outgoing confirmation cannot trigger the same handler again.
